# Modeling Report: A-cumcm-2022-c-002

## Problem Framing

The case is CUMCM 2022 C, “古代玻璃制品的成分分析与鉴别.” The modeling objective is to distinguish two archaeological glass classes:

- high-potassium glass;
- lead-barium glass.

Observed predictors are chemical-component proportions. The data are compositional: component proportions should sum to approximately 100%, but measurement error is allowed. A record is valid when the component sum lies in `[85%, 105%]`.

The supplied summary does not include numbered subquestion text. Therefore, this report defines the common analysis contract; exact q1/q2/... outputs are pending confirmation from the benchmark owner.

